# Introducing Nonlinear Pricing into Consumer Choice Theory.

**Authors:** DeSalvo, Joseph S., Huq, Mobinul

## Abstract
Describes and contrasts nonlinear and linear pricing in consumer choice theory. Discusses the types of nonlinear pricing: block-declining tariff, two-part tariff, three-part tariff, and quality discounts or premia. States that understanding nonlinear pricing enhances student comprehension of consumer choice theory. Suggests teaching the concept in graduate microeconomics or mathematical economics courses. (JEH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ675459

